## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical Dataflow streaming design with real-world concerns like per-tenant isolation and observability.

## Key Concepts
- Pub/Sub ingestion
- Dataflow streaming transforms and DoFn-like validation
- Per-tenant BigQuery datasets and environment isolation
- Idempotency/dedup and basic monitoring

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-Dataflow DoFn for validation
function validateEvent(record){
  if(!record.event_id || !record.tenant_id) throw new Error("Invalid");
  if(!record.event_ts) record.event_ts = Date.now();
  return record;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test idempotency under message replay?
- How would you cap cost for a high-volume tenant?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses real-time streaming design, multi-tenant isolation, data residency, and production-grade reliability in GCP.

## Key Concepts
- Pub/Sub exact-once hints, Dataflow streaming, stateful processing
- Per-tenant IAM, separate buckets/service accounts, residency
- Hybrid scoring: rules engine + Vertex AI
- Dead-letter routing, canary deployments, observability

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: streaming transform sketch
class ScoreDoFn {
  process(event) {
    const score = ruleScore(event) + mlScore(event);
    emit({ tenant: event.tenantId, id: event.id, score, ts: event.ts });
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate idempotence and exactly-once guarantees at scale?
- How would you test tenant isolation across regions and handle schema evolution?
